# The first touch of the crown shard (one-shot per save). Opened from code
# (TSC_ShardTracker) the moment a colonist first has the shard in hand;
# {PLAYER} is that pawn. The Act 2 title card follows when this closes.

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_ShardRush

== start ==
The shard is lighter than it should be, and colder than the cave.

The moment {PLAYER}'s fingers close on it, something answers: a rush, wrist to spine to skull, like plunging into a winter river.

Then it passes. Almost. A cold weight settles behind the breastbone and stays there.

Broken or not, the piece still carries some of the power that the whole crown once granted.

Behind {PLAYER}, in the black marble, the folded hands come apart.

* [Close your hand around it.] -> end
